      "problem": "${(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $2$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $2:$\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}=\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, using ${3}^{2}=9$ and ${5}^{2}=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=\\frac{9}{25}.\n$$",
